            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0742" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3831/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-19T09:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1935—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:25 a.m]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Reference to Legation’s despatch No. 565, March 12,<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d658-f1"/> regarding trade agreement, and situation resulting from
                    French representations. I am planning to leave here March 21 and an indication
                    of Department’s attitude on this question as well as bank sale plan<anchor
                        n="18" xml:id="d658-f2"/> would be helpful before final interview with
                    President noon tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
